  "source": "knowledge/project/plant-palette-slices.md row b3 and the chunk 2 drift check (2026-11-15) section 3; ux-inventory P39 (one family, water needs) and board MainMore (Balance: things to weigh, not holes); owner rows 'warn, never hide' and 'inform, don't block'. A plant's water need is the factAt water_need fact (ADR-6) through source.ts waterNeed, the one classifier: its drought tolerance when recorded (High: dry, Medium: medium, Low or None: needs regular water), else its moisture use (Low: dry, Medium: medium, High: needs regular water), else not recorded. Owner 2026-11-15: the Low/None group reads 'Needs regular water'; the v14 boards (approved 2026-11-18, later) call those plants 'thirsty' in the mixed form ('Water needs: one thirsty plant among N recorded', PaletteMore), and the board wins; the family line keeps 3 plants and 25 %; no water all-clear line (the water line shows only when needs are mixed or too few are recorded; otherwise the plants with no water need recorded are said on their own, review b3f-4). Plants not checked (a guest list unread, a plant on none of the climate's lists: input 'unchecked') count in m, never a judgement of part of the palette as the whole. Written by PP-B stream b3. v14 pf-b fix round 1 (boards PaletteMore, MainMore): every water form names the plants not recorded, so its members are those plants (the last 'missing' of the mixed form's members); the mixed form ('water-mix', board 'Water needs: one thirsty plant among N recorded') lists the plants needing regular water, then the dry-loving ones, then those between ('medium'), then those not recorded; with no other water line the plants not recorded are said on their own ('not-recorded-named').",
